---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii4_63",
  "series": "Band II 4 (1701 - 1707)",
  "seq": 63,
  "text": "<p> [[204.15]] <b>63. DAMARIS LADY MASHAM AN LEIBNIZ</p>\n<p> [[204.16]] Oates, 29. März (9. April) 1704. [56.67.] </b></p>\n<p> [[205.9]] S^#'r Oates 29 March 1704 </p>\n<p> [[205.10]] Thō I am not in the Number of those who can confirm the advantageous Idea you have of\n[[205.11]] English Ladys yet I have been too much conversant amongst Learned Men not to have\n[[205.12]] contracted (so far as I am capable of it) a Just Value for them or to have been ignorant of the\n[[205.13]] rank you hold in the Commonwealth of Letters. This has dispos'd me long since to entertain\n[[205.14]] with Pleasure any Occasion of testifying a great Respect for you; and has lately suggested to me\n[[205.15]] that my Fathers <k>Intellectual System</k> might, possibly, not be unacceptable to you. The\n[[205.16]] esteem you express for that Work pleases me very much both on this account, and also as it is a\n[[205.17]] new Confirmation to me of the Worth of that Performance. </p>\n<p> [[205.18]] I should be glad to have a farther view into the Intellectual World; and would therefore\n[[205.19]] willingly have right Conceptions of the System you propose. To this Purpose upon the receit of\n[[205.20]] your obliging Letter, I look'd into the Article of <k>Rorarius</k> in the first Edition of M^#'r Bayls\n[[205.21]] Dictionarie (not haveing the 2^#'d by me) and being by his quotation of you there, directed to the\n[[205.22]] <i>Journal des Savans</i> 1695 I read what is there publish'd of it. </p>\n<p> [[205.23]] Perhaps my not being accustom'd to such abstract Speculations made me not well\n[[205.24]] comprehend what you say there of <b><i>Formes</i></b>, upon which I think you build your Hypothesis: for\n[[205.25]] (as it seemes to me) you sometimes call them <b><i>Forces Primitives</b></i>, sometimes <b><i>des Ames</b></i>\n[[205.26]] sometimes <b><i>Formes constitutives des substances</b></i>, and sometimes <b><i>Substances</i></b> themselves;\n[[205.27]] but such yet as are neither Spirit, nor matter whence I confess I have no cleare Idea of what\n[[205.28]] you call <b><i>Formes</i></b>. </p>\n<p> [[205.29]] That a man whose Correspondence is so highly esteem'd as yours by all the Learned men\n[[205.30]] of Europe should employ any of his valuable Moments in the instruction of an Ignorant Woman\n[[205.31]] is what I should not perhaps presume to importune you for, if your character was known to me\n[[206.1]] onely as a Learned Man; for those who are far advanced in Learned Studies, and high\n[[206.2]] Speculations may think themselves excus'd from such a Condescention; but you I am confident\n[[206.3]] would not contemne the most Ignorant Lover of Truth; were I not secur'd by my sex of a\n[[206.4]] favorable distinction from the obligeing Civilitie of a Man Conversant in Courts. </p>\n<p> [[206.5]] I take the libertie therefore to request the favour of you that you will by some explication\n[[206.6]] or definition of them help me to Conceive what your <b><i>Formes</b></i> are; for I cannot but desire to\n[[206.7]] understand a Systeme recommended to me not onely by the eminence of its Author, but\n[[206.8]] particularly also as tending to inlarge our Idea of the Divine Perfections, and the Beautie of his\n[[206.9]] Works. If you please to add in short the Sum of your Answers to M^#'r Bayles objections in his\n[[206.10]] second edition of his Dictionarie it will be an Additional Obligation in giveing me still further\n[[206.11]] Light into this matter. </p>\n<p> [[206.12]] I have order'd my Fathers <i>Discourse concerning the Lords Supper</i> to be sent you together\n[[206.13]] with his <i>Intellectual System</i> in the same vol: the Value you express for the Author makes me\n[[206.14]] think you will not dislike to look into anything of his and thō this Treatise was writ when he\n[[206.15]] was a Young Man, yet it was Highly commended by our Famous Selden. </p>\n<p> [[206.16]] You will much oblige me in accepting of this Book as from one who is with great Esteem\n[[206.17]] and Respect </p>\n<p> [[206.18]] S^#'r Your very Humble Servant Da Masham. </p>\n<p> [[206.19]] M^#'r Locke (whose company I am so Happy as to injoy in my Familie) desires me to present\n[[206.20]] you his Humble Service. </p>\n",
  "number": "63.",
  "title": "DAMARIS LADY MASHAM AN LEIBNIZ",
  "date": "Oates, 29. März (9. April) 1704. [56.67.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:63. DAMARIS LADY MASHAM AN LEIBNIZ Oates, 29. März (9. April) 1704. [56.67.] S^#'r Oates 29 March 1704 Thō I am not in the Number of those who can confirm the advantageous Idea you have of English Ladys yet I have been too much conversant amongst Learned Men not to have contracted (so far as I am ca...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>